<Base title="Architecture | Kubernautic"><section class="shell page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURE / GUIDING PRINCIPLES</span><h1>Open foundations.<br/><span class="gradient-text">Controlled intelligence.</span></h1><p>Our design direction connects Kubernetes visibility, AI-supported interpretation and explicit operational governance. This page describes the intended architecture, not a claim that every component is already shipped.</p></section><section class="shell section single-section"><div class="content-grid"><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">⌁</div><h3>Signal layer</h3><p>Kubernetes API, events, workload inventory, logs and telemetry as authorized.</p></article><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">◈</div><h3>Context layer</h3><p>Infrastructure relationships, application state, timing and causal hypotheses.</p></article><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">✳</div><h3>Intelligence layer</h3><p>Agentic reasoning and interpretable recommendations for operators.</p></article><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">◇</div><h3>Governance layer</h3><p>Policy checks, scoped access, approvals and auditability.</p></article><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">⬡</div><h3>Console layer</h3><p>A guided interface for exploration, operational context and next steps.</p></article><article class="content-tile"><div class="tile-icon">↗</div><h3>Open integration</h3><p>Architecture that can evolve with the Kubernetes and OpenKubes ecosystem.</p></article></div></section><CTA/></Base>
